    "$schema_note": "TERRAFRONT region decor templates (W9 world-decor lane; W10 decor-collision). Per-tier layout computed once per region by World/TFRegionDecor — the layout is role-agnostic and deterministic on BOTH server and client; visuals spawn on viewer roles only. offset = [x, z] meters from region center (+x east, +z north); yaw in DEGREES (Transform.rotation is degrees; the RADIANS rule is PhysicsBody-only — TFWorldCollision converts for Jolt). terrainAlign true (default) snaps each piece to TerrainHeightAt at its own column; false uses the region-center height (level runs, e.g. pipelines). material optional — default is the neutral/faction structure material (skyanchor pieces tint by homeFaction, everything else neutral). collide (W10, default FALSE) — true gives the piece one static Jolt OBB from its model bounds on BOTH roles (buildings only; keep small props, pipelines and holo signs walk-through; scatter props never collide). scatter = per-region seeded prop ring (seed = RegionId, deterministic across roles): count [min,max], radius [min,max] meters from center. Code enforces >= clearanceM from every capturePoint/spawn/vehicleTerminal (collidable pieces against EVERY region's points, demoted to visual-only on violation) and caps total pieces at 20 per region. collideParts (W11 API; data re-authored W12 after the leg-cage stall) = MODEL-LOCAL boxes {offset:[x,y,z] box center, size:[x,y,z] FULL size, yawDeg local yaw} that REPLACE the whole-model OBB (authoring parts implies collide:true; max 5 per piece). Authoring rules: keep gate archways >= 2.2m wide x 2.6m tall clear; NEVER author cage patterns (the W11 four-leg watchtower trapped bots between its own legs — use ONE convex central column; players cannot stand inside the tower base, accepted approximation); parts whose bottom sits >= 2m up (lintels, gantry spans) are walk-under. TFRegionDecor validates after layout: parts of DIFFERENT pieces pinching a <1.2m corridor demote the smaller piece, and every capturePoint must keep a >= 120-degree open ground approach (blockers demoted).",
